# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Next copies everything in public/ to the export
# root, so this ships as out/_headers. GitHub Pages ignores the file, which is why
# it was safe to add before the host cutover.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here yet. A correct one has to allow connect-src for
# the Supabase project and img-src for flagcdn.com, resources.premierleague.com
# and fantasy.premierleague.com. Worth adding, but not folded into a hosting
# migration: if the crests stopped loading you could not tell which change did it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Next content-hashes every filename under here, so a stale copy can never be
# served for changed content and a one-year immutable cache is safe.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
